  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) at 0.527 acc, modestly above RNA-only (0.485) and far above image-only (0.208). Fusion strategy (concat vs weighted) shows negligible difference. The single most important untested design axis is whether multiprofile + aggregation provides additional signal beyond a single profile. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improve performance in the current best multimodal setup? config_018 is a direct, minimal extension of config_016—same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), same image encoder (resnet50), same fusion (concat)—changing only the profile/aggregation dimension. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation cleanly. Why best next: With only 4 experiments completed, understanding whether multiprofile aggregation is beneficial is foundational before investing budget in alternative RNA encoders or image encoders. If multiprofile helps, it opens a productive direction (configs 019-027); if it does not, we can focus budget on encoder choices instead."
}

